      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "Multiplying rotates and stretches",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s4",
      "narration": "Multiplying by z rotates by its angle and stretches by its modulus. So raising z to the power n rotates by n times the angle and stretches by the modulus to the power n. De Moivre's theorem packages exactly that: z to the n equals r to the n times cos n-theta plus i sin n-theta.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "reAxis",
            "kind": "line",
            "stroke": "#1a1a1a",
            "width": 2,
            "x1": 80,
            "x2": 880,
            "y1": 300,
            "y2": 300
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "z",
            "kind": "arrow",
            "stroke": "#1f7a3a",
            "width": 4,
            "x1": 480,
            "x2": 640,
            "y1": 300,
            "y2": 220
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "multLab",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "× z: rotate by θ, scale by r",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 140
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "z2",
            "kind": "arrow",
            "stroke": "#1a56db",
            "width": 4,
            "x1": 480,
            "x2": 700,
            "y1": 300,
            "y2": 120
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "demoivre",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 40,
            "tex": "z^n = r^n(\\cos n\\theta + i\\sin n\\theta)",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 420
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "dmLab",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 26,
            "text": "de Moivre: powers turn multiplication into angles",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 500
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7200,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "z2"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 8000,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "De Moivre: multiply the lengths, add the angles"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "The classic slip: angles wrap around",
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "One slip to dodge. Take theta equals 100 degrees: three times theta is 300 degrees, but the principal argument of z cubed is not 300 degrees. Principal values wrap into minus 180 to 180 degrees, so the argument is minus 60 degrees. The toolkit: modulus is Pythagoras from the origin, de Moivre turns powers into multiplied lengths and added angles, and Arg always lands inside minus 180 to 180 degrees.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#b00020",
            "id": "mis",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 36,
            "text": "Misconception:",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "setup",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 30,
            "text": "θ = 100°, n = 3 gives nθ = 300°",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 200
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#b00020",
            "id": "slip",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "\\arg(z^3) \\ne 300^\\circ",
            "x": 140,
            "y": 290
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "fix",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "\\mathrm{Arg}(z^3) = -60^\\circ",
            "x": 140,
            "y": 375
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "wrapLab",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 28,
            "text": "principal values wrap into (−180°, 180°]",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 460
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5800,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "fix"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6600,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Angles wrap around; only the principal value is Arg"
        }
      ]
    }
